      #text(size: 8.8pt)[
        We introduce a closed-form, zero-backpropagation, zero-corpus method for surgically grafting brand-new concepts into a pretrained large language model using only *one unused embedding row and four reclaimed CJK SwiGLU neurons* (`33,280` floats, *`0.00083%`* of `Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507`).
        Our construction combines four geometric primitives:
        (1) _kind-base grafting_, showing that although passive in-context declarations fail to bind domain-specific modifier twists, a single Layer-0 embedding graft dynamically routes downstream twists across Layers 6–36 and yields a `10/10` behavioral double dissociation;
        (2) _RMSNorm–tied-head scale asymmetry_ paired with an orthogonal _private address_ ($bold(e)_G = gamma r_"ref" (cos theta hat(bold(e))_K + sin theta hat(bold(u))_perp)$), which preserves `81–100%` of downstream comprehension via Layer-0 RMSNorm scale-invariance while reducing adversarial near-neighbor KL by *`4,503×–275,496×`* via exponential softmax suppression;
        (3) _implicit cone-bias SwiGLU self-gating_ ($bold(w)_"gate" = s(bold(k) - tau bold(b))$), creating sharp thresholded key–value detectors inside bias-free MLPs ($669 times$–$29,475 times$ fit SNR, $<= 0.0005%$ wrong-attribute trap leakage); and
        (4) _multi-scale linear attribute superposition_ (Read) paired with _orthogonal private-address targeting_ (Write).
        Stacking two distinct concepts simultaneously (`Icelandic flavor` and `Japanese sound`, `0.0017%` of parameters) unlocks zero-shot multi-hop recall (_Reykjavik_ Rank `#1`, _Tokyo_ Rank `#4`, _Icelandic/Japanese_ Rank `#6`), achieves `39–55%` mean Rank-`#1` unseen naming recall with $<= 10^(-6)$ cross-concept bleed, and incurs only *`0.00087` nats* cumulative out-of-sample KL.
      ]
    ]
  ]
]

