= Limitations & Planned Full-Paper Work

We highlight three honest limits of this technical note that define our upcoming full paper:
1. _Attribute strength vs. parent-kind dilution:_ Strong early superposition (`read_alphas=[1.5, 1.2, 0.8]`) achieves `Reykjavik #1` and `Tokyo #4`, but dilutes non-origin behavioral preference (`Behav B`: $+2.79 -> +0.56$ for `G1`, $-2.97 -> -1.31$ for `G2`, retaining a `1.88` log-odds gap). Orthogonalizing Read payloads against $hat(bold(e))_K$ and mapping the `read_alphas` Pareto curve is an immediate next step.
2. _4-shot Write surface coverage:_ A sharp `gate_tau=0.50` guarantees $<= 5 times 10^(-6)$ trap leakage, but `2–3/6` syntactically distant unseen naming paraphrases fall just below threshold ($bold(k)^top bold(x) approx 0.63 "–" 0.70$).
3. _Scale & baselines:_ This note validates $K=2$ concepts on one 4B architecture. Our full paper will measure stacking capacity across $K in {1, 2, 5, 10, 20}$ diverse concepts (including non-geographic attributes), replicate across a second model family (`Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct` / `Qwen3.5-4B`), and benchmark directly against matched-budget gradient fine-tuning (Adam on the same slots/prompts).

